# Two programs have a source PACKAGE directory with the same name as the
# program, so the entry above matches the directory as well as the binary
# and silently hides the package. A trailing slash matches directories
# only, so these re-include the directory while the entry above still
# ignores the compiled file. Without them a newly added module in either
# package is invisible to git -- the same class of accident that got
# collatz/doom/othello2 committed in ce380ff4.
!c64/c64/
!pylot/pylot/

# The root .gitignore's "Debugging and Output Cruft" rules are aimed at
# scratch files at the repo root, and reach into this vendored corpus
# where the same names mean something else entirely. Patterns in a
# deeper .gitignore win, so scope them back out here:
#
#   *.txt  hid 101 TRACKED files -- all 83 CMakeLists.txt plus every
#          testdata fixture (maze.txt, top95.txt, cornellbox.txt, ...).
#          In this tree .txt is input data, not a scratch log.
#   core   hid tarsalzp/com/github/tarsa/tarsalzp/core/, a Python
#          PACKAGE, all 7 modules. The rule means core dumps; the
#          trailing slash re-includes the directory, which a file-level
#          negation cannot do once a parent directory is excluded.
#
# Both were silent, and the reason is worth stating precisely: .gitignore
# does not affect files that are already TRACKED, so every one of those
# 108 kept showing its edits normally and nothing looked wrong. The cost
# was on NEW files. Measured: a fresh adatron/testdata/newfixture.txt is
# invisible to `git status` without these negations and shows as `??`
# with them. So a new fixture or a new module in tarsalzp's core/ could
# be written, tested, and lost -- git never mentions it.
!*.txt
!core/

# Runtime outputs the corpus programs write into their own directories.
# Named individually because the un-ignoring above deliberately treats
# .txt in this tree as data: neural1 saves its trained net with
# open('jets.txt','wb') (neural1.py:154) and rdb sets
# self.logfile = "rebuild_db.log.txt" (rdb.py:78).
neural1/jets.txt
rdb/rebuild_db.log.txt
